tools/shadowbench/out/

# --- Claude Code: track shared harness config (.claude/agents, .claude/README.md, .claude/settings.json)
#     but never the per-clone RUNTIME scratch (these were previously only in the local, uncommitted
#     .git/info/exclude). The github-sync mirror strips the whole .claude/ tree regardless (denylist step).
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/routines/.state/
.claude/worktrees/
# claim-before-touch session-hygiene locks (TG-81) live under .claude/worktrees/.claims/. The line above
# already excludes them; this explicit rule keeps a claim from EVER reaching a commit even if that parent
# is one day narrowed (the frontend/dist un-ignore below is why we now anchor these belt-and-suspenders).
.claude/worktrees/.claims/
.claude/checkpoints/
.claude/mailbox/
.claude/agent-registry.json
.claude/agent-memory-local
.claude/first-run
.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json
guardallow

# Local build/analysis artifacts that keep getting swept up by `git add -A`. They are large, they are
# not source, and gitleaks flags benchmark payloads inside them as generic API keys.
/evalgate
/judgecal
/diagscore
tools/shadowbench/*.bak
tools/shadowbench/*.quarantined-*.jsonl
tools/shadowbench/scorecard.quarantined-oldcode.jsonl

# --- JavaScript dependency trees and build output, unanchored on purpose (TG-257).
#
# ADR-0015 deleted the unreachable React frontend/. The commit that did it ("one console — delete the
# unreachable React frontend/", 4b0e9763 in !765) ALSO deleted the ignore rules that had been hiding that
# build's output — so frontend/ went from 52 tracked files to 6,706, of which 6,647 were node_modules, and
# 98.5 MB of dependency tree sat on main for four days. Every clone and CI checkout carried it.
#
# These are unanchored (no leading slash) precisely because the rules they replace were not: /dist/ above
# matches only the repository root and never covered frontend/dist. deploy/tracked_tree_test.go is the
# part that survives someone deleting these lines again, which is exactly how this happened.
node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Rust build artifacts from running the sidecar's own test suite locally
deploy/claude-proxy/target/
# Local TLS material for the sidecar/claude-proxy. TG-414 deleted the tls/.gitignore that had protected
# proxy.key when it retired the off-box scaffolding; keep the (never-committed) private key out of the
# public mirror and out of `git add -A`. deploy/tracked_tree_test.go guards against re-tracking.
deploy/claude-proxy/tls/
/estatedoc-ingest
